<title>USA: Sun cuts U.S. posted crude prices 75 cts.</title>
<headline>Sun cuts U.S. posted crude prices 75 cts.</headline>
<dateline>NEW YORK 1997-02-21</dateline>
<text>
<p>Sun Co Inc said it had lowered the price it will pay for U.S. crude oil by 75 cents, effective Friday.</p>
<p>The decrease brings the new price for U.S. benchmark grade West Texas Intermediate to $19.50 a barrel and West Texas Sour to $17.00 a barrel.</p>
<p>Light Louisiana sweet crude is now $19.50 and Oklahoma sweet is $19.50.</p>
<p>--New York Energy Desk, +1 212 859 1623</p>
</text>
